{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They carry it. It cannot move.</b> In its place." "<b>It does not remove.</b> A transitive verb: it cannot move itself from its place. Or it is an intransitive verb, but the first is correct." "<b>It cries out.</b> It draws after it [the meaning of] 'with it'; and so too הוא ומצרתו יצעק (it and its distress cry out)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:18.442464765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}